12
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
Coming to America is a 1988 American romantic comedy film directed by John Landis, based on a
story originally created by Eddie Murphy, written by David Sheffield and Barry W.

13
01:12:25,714 --> 01:12:31,714
Blaustein, and starring Murphy (in various roles), Arsenio Hall (also in various
roles), James Earl Jones, John Amos, Madge Sinclair, and Shari Headley.

14
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
It tells the story of Akeem Joffer, the crown prince of the fictional African nation of Zamunda who travels to the United States in the hopes
of finding a woman he can marry and will love him for who he is, not for his status or for having been trained to please him.

15
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
The film was released in the United States on June 29, 1988, and
received generally positive reviews from critics.

16
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
It was also a box-office success, grossing an estimated
$288.8–$350 million on a $36 million budget.

17
01:34:42,857 --> 01:34:48,857
In 1989, a pilot for a planned spin-off television series was
made, although this was never picked up for a series.

18
01:40:17,142 --> 01:40:23,142
A sequel to the film—Coming 2 America—was released on March 4, 2021.

19
01:45:51,428 --> 01:45:57,428
The film explores themes of new york city, fast food
restaurant, prince, fake identity, heir to the throne.

20
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
